WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.260
Thanks for tuning in to Planetarian Daily, episode 88 for June 13th, 2026.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.040
Let's see what the latest research is telling us.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.140
Among nearly 10,000 children,

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.700
socioeconomic status showed the largest associations

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.180
with brain structure out of 649 environmental,

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.480
behavioral, health, and socioeconomic factors.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.100
The strongest links appeared in primary,

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.660
motor, and sensory cortex,

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.560
and held across multiple imaging modalities.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:32.060
Lower status aligned with consistent shifts in cortical organization

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.060
that remained independent of the other variables measured.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:38.680
The work comes from direct mapping of these relationships

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.540
in a large pediatric cohort.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.820
Now, shifting from structural brain changes

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.080
to how social conditions alter molecular aging clocks.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:52.900
A meta-analysis of 140 studies covering nearly 66,000 people

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:57.040
linked lower socioeconomic status and discrimination exposure

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.940
to faster epigenetic aging.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:03.320
The bio-social team at the Max Planck Institute for Human Development

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.620
led the analysis with Columbia University collaborators.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.900
Aging was measured through methylation patterns in the epigenome.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:16.340
Remember, the show covered aging and longevity biology on episode 87.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.600
This work adds population level evidence that social exposures

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:24.340
shift the same molecular clocks tracked in intervention trials.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:29.380
The integration supplies direct evidence from the same clocks used in those trials.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:34.060
Now, moving from population level aging to practical lab tools

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.740
that could test ways to slow it.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.000
Researchers developed a culture dog muscle cells

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.820
that allow early testing of new treatments before animal studies begin.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:47.240
The cells retain key functional properties of native canine muscle

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.700
and respond to candidate compounds in predictable ways.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:56.040
This platform reduces the number of dogs needed for initial safety and efficacy checks.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:01.240
The approach supplies a standardized starting point for identifying which molecules merit

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.400
further investigation.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:06.780
The platform keeps contractile and metabolic properties intact,

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.080
giving an earlier filter for compounds.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:14.360
It directly supports regenerative medicine work by shrinking the gap between cell assays

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.680
and whole animal models.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:20.280
Researchers at the HUNARIN Biological Research Center identified

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:25.900
specific surface proteins that let certain gut bacterial phases bind directly to human cells.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:32.040
The proteins promote uptake into intestinal tissues and longer retention within the gastrointestinal

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:36.180
tract. The work appeared in nature communications and demonstrates that

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:41.440
phages can form physical interactions with host tissues rather than remaining solely within the

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:42.560
microbial compartment.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:47.520
These binding events create potential routes for targeted phage delivery systems.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:53.360
The findings also suggest new possibilities for microbiome modulation strategies

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.040
that rely on engineered surface interactions.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:01.040
On a different note, comic book readers retain plot connections better

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.020
when the material appears on paper rather than tablets.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:10.180
The tactile and spatial layout of pages supplies fixed reference points that reduce memory

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:15.620
load during later recall. Participants showed clearer retention of narrative connections when

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:19.540
the physical version supplied consistent page positions and edge textures.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:22.740
No equivalent anchors exist on flat screens.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:28.180
The findings comes from direct comparison of the same material presented in both formats.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:32.380
The result is format specific rather than content specific.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:37.860
A team that included the Institute Catalan de Paleontologia Miquel Crucifont

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:43.200
described a new Amphysianid species named Paluto Cion Moia Solai.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.020
From fossil material recovered at else casotes in Spain.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:54.140
The medium-sized bear dog lived approximately 15.9 million years ago during the early middle

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:59.880
mayocene. The species name honors paleontologist Salvador Moia Solai.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:05.520
The discovery supplies additional detail on carnivore diversity present in that interval.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:11.480
The fossils were analyzed through standard comparative morphology and stratigraphic correlation.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:16.540
Now, here's something most people get wrong about how trees build carbon stores.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:22.180
Most people picture trees steadily adding wood whenever leaves are green and photosynthesis is running.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:29.040
In reality, many species halt new growth by mid-summer even while carbon fixation continues.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:32.280
Right now, as you walk past an oak in late summer,

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.720
its leaves may still be pulling carbon dioxide from the air.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:38.480
Yet the trunk and roots are no longer expanding.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:44.140
One memorable detail is that this growth stoppage can occur while photosynthesis remains

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:49.460
active for weeks or months afterward. The practical takeaway is that forest carbon

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:54.420
accounting must separate photosynthesis measurements from actual biomass gain.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:05:00.280
Watch for upcoming studies that pair seasonal growth rings with real-time gas exchange data

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:05.740
to refine those models. University of Oregon researchers combined field measurements

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:11.620
with modeling across slopes of different gradients and found that hilly and mountainous landscapes

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:16.440
hold substantially larger soil carbon reserves than earlier estimates assumed.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:22.700
Steeper terrain promotes deeper burial of organic matter, together with slower rates of decomposition.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:29.020
The work indicates that global carbon budgets will require upward revision once these higher storage

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:34.300
rates are incorporated. The measurements were taken across multiple slope classes to capture

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:40.380
variation in burial depth and microbial activity. The results applied directly to improved accounting

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:46.840
of terrestrial carbon sinks. Next up, sediment records show the Gulf Stream moved farther north during

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:54.340
a global cooling event 12,900 years ago. UCL researchers use those records to document the

00:05:54.340 --> 00:06:00.660
current position directly for the first time. The shift temporarily changed temperature and nutrient

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:06.860
patterns in the northwest Atlantic. Similar repositioning remains possible under ongoing climate

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:13.320
change. The work provides the first direct documentation of such a position change. A science study

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:19.660
led by the Leibniz Institute of Freshwater Ecology and Inland Fisheries modeled how both the volume

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:25.720
and velocity of water moving through European landscapes control nitrate delivery to rivers and

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:32.140
groundwater. Faster transit times reduce the window available for microbial processing and therefore

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:38.440
increase export of nitrogen to downstream waters. The analysis covered the continent and showed that

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:44.120
climate-driven shifts in hydrology will alter pollution patterns even if fertilizer application

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:50.560
rates stay constant. The model integrated flow path length and residence time across varied terrain

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:56.960
types. The findings highlight hydrology as an independent driver separate from nutrient input levels.

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:02.660
From past ocean shifts to modern infection control practices in extreme environments.

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:10.940
Across 196 NASA missions from Apollo through 2024, infections occurred around launch in 15% of

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:17.040
cases. None resulted in medical evacuation, severe in-orbit illness or lasting health effects.

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:23.780
The pre-flight quarantine program appears responsible for containing spread. Data cover both short

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:29.340
and long duration flights. From contained human environments to new materials that convert

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:35.560
mechanical stress into signals. A new zinc oxide material produces light under mechanical stress

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:42.040
without relying on rare earth elements. The mechanical luminescent compound works at room temperature

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:48.320
and could serve in self-powered sensors. Applications range from biomedical monitoring to infrastructure

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:54.960
strain detection. Simpler composition lowers cost and supply chain risks compared with earlier

00:07:54.960 --> 00:08:02.060
formulations. From sensor materials to nuclear-based timekeeping. Two independent teams built functional

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:09.240
nuclear clocks using the thorium 229 nucleus. The Chingwa University and Vienna Center for Quantum

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:14.400
Science and Technology groups each demonstrated timekeeping based on nuclear transitions.

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:20.980
These devices may eventually exceed the precision of current atomic clocks. The work marks the

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:28.100
transition from theoretical proposal to operational instrument. University of Birmingham physicist Giovanni

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:34.280
Barontini constructed a laboratory model system in which time emerges solely from the dynamics of

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:41.000
interacting particles. The setup published in physical review research tracks temporal flow without

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:46.980
any external clock device. The experiment tests whether time can arise as a derived property from

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:52.460
particle interactions rather than serving as a fundamental input. The approach may help clarify

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:58.420
connections between quantum behavior and the emergence of macroscopic time. Further refinements are

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:03.960
planned to explore additional parameter regimes. From precision measurement to detection of emerging

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:09.660
chemical threats. Researchers trained models on known fentanyl structures to forecast chemical

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:16.000
features of more than 1 billion possible variants. The method identify spectral patterns that could

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:22.440
allow detection of previously uncatalog analogues. Published findings focus on expanding reference

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:28.740
libraries for forensic and clinical screening. The approach addresses the rapid emergence of new synthetic

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:34.800
opioids. Keep an eye on further refinements to the thorium 229 nuclear clock demonstrations,

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:40.940
expected in coming months. That covers today's science and health news. Share this with someone

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:46.720
who's curious about the latest research. I'm Patrick and Vancouver. See you next time. And before

